{%- doc -%}
  Dawn-native quick-add for hz cards — Phase 13 round 3.

  EXTRACTION of Dawn snippets/card-product.liquid:148-243 (the
  quick_add == 'standard' region), markup/classes/ids verbatim. RULING
  (Nathan, serve gate 2026-07-07): "Quick add is still not behaving like
  Dawn's" — Dawn's native quick-add is live store-wide and structurally
  different from the ported Horizon modal (which can never show M&P's
  customized <product-info> picker). Ruled: Dawn machinery wholesale on hz
  cards + pure-Dawn mobile (no mobile_quick_add setting — Dawn's trigger is
  server-side gated and always visible at both breakpoints). The Horizon
  quick-add subsystem stays in-repo as ported vocabulary, unwired from M&P
  card surfaces (see snippets/quick-add.liquid header).

  Behavior (all Dawn, live-proven on collection grids):
  - Multi-variant or qty rules → modal-opener → <quick-add-modal>
    (assets/quick-add.js) fetches the product URL, injects the REAL M&P
    <product-info> — picker incl. swatch_message, buy buttons, "View full
    details" — pickup/zoom modals stripped, ids renamed quickadd-{id},
    data-update-url="false".
  - Single-variant, no qty rules → direct <product-form> POST
    (assets/product-form.js); disabled + .sold-out-message when unavailable.
  - Add from modal → modal closes FIRST, then cart-notification/drawer
    (Rebuy) opens (product-form.js:79-92).

  Deviations from the source region:
  - Parameterized: card_product → product; the section id is the section_id
    render param (incl. data-section-id — stock reads section.id there; no
    JS on this path consumes it).
  - The quick_add == 'standard' gate lives at the CALL SITE
    (blocks/_product-card-gallery reads section.settings.quick_add), as does
    the Badge-Coming Soon unless-wrap (card-product.liquid:147 parity).
  - The {% if horizontal_quick_add %} legs are TRIMMED (Dawn's horizontal
    card layout flag — no hz consumer; restore from the source region if a
    horizontal hz card ever exists).
  - aria-labelledby's second id (title-{section_id}-{product.id}) is a Dawn
    card-title id hz cards don't emit; kept verbatim (the button's own id
    resolves).
  - The .quick-add wrapper carries color-{{ settings.card_color_scheme }}
    gradient (serve fix, Nathan's punchlist FAIL 2026-07-08 — "should be a
    white square with a black +"): on live Dawn the button sits inside the
    card's scheme wrapper (card-product.liquid puts
    color-{{ settings.card_color_scheme }} on the card; live = scheme-2 →
    --color-button 255,255,255 / --color-button-text 0,0,0). hz cards have
    no Dawn card-scheme ancestor, so without this the .button fell back to
    dark scheme values (black square). Same global setting Dawn reads —
    merchant changes track live. The wrapper's painted scheme background is
    fully covered by the opaque button (wrapper auto-sizes to the button).

  Asset deps: quick-add.css + quick-add.js + product-form.js are loaded by
  the gated hosts (hz-product-list / hz-product-recommendations — the
  main-collection-product-grid.liquid:13-20 pattern); global.js
  (ModalDialog / modal-opener / HTMLUpdateUtility) is theme-global.

  @param {object} product - The product object
  @param {string} section_id - The section ID (Dawn product_form_id shape)
{%- enddoc -%}
{% assign product_form_id = 'quick-add-' | append: section_id | append: product.id %}
<div class="quick-add no-js-hidden color-{{ settings.card_color_scheme }} gradient">
  {%- liquid
    assign qty_rules = false
    if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.quantity_rule.min > 1 or product.selected_or_first_available_variant.quantity_rule.max != null or product.selected_or_first_available_variant.quantity_rule.increment > 1
      assign qty_rules = true
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if product.variants_count > 1 or qty_rules -%}
    <modal-opener data-modal="#QuickAdd-{{ product.id }}">
      <button
        id="{{ product_form_id }}-submit"
        type="submit"
        name="add"
        class="quick-add__submit button"
        aria-haspopup="dialog"
        aria-labelledby="{{ product_form_id }}-submit title-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
        data-product-url="{{ product.url }}"
      >
        <span class="icon-wrap">
          {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>
        {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
      </button>
    </modal-opener>
    <quick-add-modal id="QuickAdd-{{ product.id }}" class="quick-add-modal">
      <div
        role="dialog"
        aria-label="{{ 'products.product.choose_product_options' | t: product_name: product.title | escape }}"
        aria-modal="true"
        class="quick-add-modal__content global-settings-popup"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        <button
          id="ModalClose-{{ product.id }}"
          type="button"
          class="quick-add-modal__toggle"
          aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
        >
          {{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </button>
        <div id="QuickAddInfo-{{ product.id }}" class="quick-add-modal__content-info"></div>
      </div>
    </quick-add-modal>
  {%- else -%}
    <product-form data-section-id="{{ section_id }}">
      {%- form 'product',
        product,
        id: product_form_id,
        class: 'form',
        novalidate: 'novalidate',
        data-type: 'add-to-cart-form'
      -%}
        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="id"
          value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
          class="product-variant-id"
          {% if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available == false %}
            disabled
          {% endif %}
        >
        <button
          id="{{ product_form_id }}-submit"
          type="submit"
          name="add"
          class="quick-add__submit button"
          aria-haspopup="dialog"
          aria-labelledby="{{ product_form_id }}-submit title-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
          aria-live="polite"
          data-sold-out-message="true"
          {% if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available == false %}
            disabled
          {% endif %}
        >
          <span class="icon-wrap">
            {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
          <span class="sold-out-message hidden">
            {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
          </span>
          {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
        </button>
      {%- endform -%}
    </product-form>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
